{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Who brought you out of the land of Egypt.</b> The bringing out is sufficient that you should be bondmen to Me. Another interpretation: since He revealed Himself at the sea as a mighty warrior and revealed Himself here as an elder full of compassion — as it says ״וּמִתַּחַת רַגְלָיו כְּמַעֲשֵׂה לִבְנַת הַסַּפִּיר״ (Exodus 24), this was before Him at the time of the bondage, and ״וּכְעֶצֶם הַשָּׁמַיִם לָטֹהַר״ — once they were redeemed — since I change in My appearances, do not say there are two domains; ״I am the one who brought you out of Egypt and at the sea.״ Another interpretation: since they heard many voices, as it says ״אֶת הַקּוֹלֹת״ — voices coming from the four directions and from the heavens and from the earth — do not say there are many domains. And why did He say in the singular ״your Elohim״? To give Moses an opening to plead as advocate in the matter of the calf — and this is what he said: ״לָמָה ה' יֶחֱרֶה אַפְּךָ בְּעַמֶּךָ״ — it was not to them that You commanded ״לֹא יִהְיֶה לְךָ אֱלֹהִים אֲחֵרִים״ but to me alone (Shemot Rabbah)." "<b>Out of the house of bondmen.</b> From the house of Pharaoh, for you were bondmen to him. Or does it mean only from a house of bondmen where they were bondmen to bondmen? Scripture says ״וַיִּפְדְּךָ מִבֵּית עֲבָדִים מִיַּד פַּרְעֹה מֶלֶךְ מִצְרָיִם״ (Deuteronomy 7) — say henceforth they were bondmen to the king and not bondmen to bondmen (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:19.284491546Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}